From 1603079ae85202d8a8c2a20e2154ae33e1c72058 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Betterr <51264180+Star-caorui@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:09:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] partnerconfig: Stop looking up a missing partner provider on
 every call

Without com.google.android.setupwizard.partner, each PartnerConfigHelper
check leaves its cached bundle null and asks the activity manager again
on the next call. Setupdesign makes these checks while binding list
items, so scrolling the setup wizard's language list made hundreds of
failed getContentProvider calls per frame.

Remember that the provider is missing once a call finds no provider for
the authority, and throw the same exception from then on without a
binder call. resetInstance() clears it.

Change-Id: Ibd778ab9de4341be89c5e88b4464535af10e8069
---
